      "writtenOn": "2022-06-15T20:04:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like I picked up a bad name. I was trying to say \"isBindingConnectionNotNull\".\n\nThere are three states for the connection:\n- null (no ServiceConnection object allocated)\n- Disconnected (e.g. before #bind called or binding failed or after receiving onServiceDisconnected())\n- Connected (binding succeed and received onServiceConnected)\n\nThis API is used to distinguish case 1 from the other two.\n\nWhile method isBindingConnectionConnected can further distinguish disconnected from connected states.\n\nSince the states are simple and common for any other standard ServiceConnection:\n- binding#connection \u003d\u003d null \u003d\u003e case 1\n- binding#connection#connected \u003d\u003d false \u003d\u003e case 2\n- binding#connection#connected \u003d\u003d true \u003d\u003e case 3\n\nSo far no explicit states are defined here.",
      "parentUuid": "fd38eaf4_e7978777",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 227,
