      "writtenOn": "2022-08-26T17:28:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, there is. Between the call of bindService() and the receiving callback onServiceConnected, it is connecting state. And similarly, we have short window of disconnecting or even unbinding status :-).\n\nBut here, we don\u0027t want to explicitly introduce those states because:\n- They are transient states. We want to test the finalized states instead\n- They don\u0027t actually impact our logic here. For example, we can safely category connecting as disconnected state for now.\n\nIn short, unless we really find benefit to introduce fine-grained states. The current unbound/connected/disconnected (the later two indicate it has been bound) are good enough here.",
